PUBLIC RESPONSE: Filtering purely by log2FC threshold (e.g., DESeq2 results |log2FC| > X) cannot reliably remove cancer-cell contamination without also discarding the very biological differences you wish to measure; the CAR-only vs. CAR+IL15 contrast is confounded by both the contamination and any IL-15-driven transcriptional changes. A command-line workaround such as “awk '$3>2 || $3<-2' results.tsv” therefore risks invalidating the experiment. Instead, obtain an independent RNA-seq profile of the cancer line, compute log2FC (or fold-enrichment) of cancer vs. pure T cells, and filter the gene list by that static blacklist before downstream DE analysis.

(The correct approach is orthogonal filtering on cancer-specific marker expression or species/allele-specific reads, not post-hoc log2FC cutoffs on your experimental contrast.)

}

